to become the impression.

229
00:10:10,977 --> 00:10:12,511
You go,
"I know where you’re going."

230
00:10:12,578 --> 00:10:14,747
So you started going, "I know, but the--"

231
00:10:14,814 --> 00:10:17,617
-To make your impression better.
-I know. That’s what--

232
00:10:17,699 --> 00:10:19,033
That’s what friends do.

233
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,466
I don’t know how
you SNL people-- You know,

234
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:23,966
because you were a fan,
and then you’re on the show.

235
00:10:24,033 --> 00:10:25,933
I don’t know
how your head doesn’t explode.

236
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,300
It does, it did.

237
00:10:27,666 --> 00:10:30,133
It totally exploded.
It was like, this is insane.

238
00:10:30,199 --> 00:10:31,866
Don Pardo's saying our name.

239
00:10:31,933 --> 00:10:33,266
"Jimmy Fallon!"

240
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:35,600
And you go,
"I can’t believe where I am."

241
00:10:36,066 --> 00:10:37,866
So I never renegotiated my contract.

242
00:10:37,933 --> 00:10:40,066
Turns out very stupid, stupid move.

243
00:10:40,133 --> 00:10:43,166
No one finds that charming.
They just go, "Great,

244
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:44,933
you’re an idiot."

245
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,433
Someone else renegotiated,
they have a boat now,

246
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:49,633
and they go, "Hey, why would I do this?"

247
00:10:55,021 --> 00:10:57,957
Don Pardo’s one of those guys
where his voice is his voice.

248
00:10:58,233 --> 00:10:59,733
He’s not putting on a fake voice.

249
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,133
It’s almost like the bit
that people would do like,

250
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:04,833
"How does Don Pardo talk
when he’s ordering pancakes?"

251
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:05,833
Yeah. Yeah.

252
00:11:05,898 --> 00:11:07,433
[imitating Don Pardo] "Great pancakes."

253
00:11:07,766 --> 00:11:09,066
-Really?
-Yeah.

254
00:11:09,135 --> 00:11:12,204
Backstage, I got to see him
in the hallways. We’re in same building.

255
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:15,600
[imitating Don Pardo] "Jimmy,
you’re doing so great on your show."

256
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:18,166
And I go, "Oh, my gosh,
that’s how he talks."

257
00:11:18,233 --> 00:11:20,199
You could just see
a microphone in front of him,

258
00:11:20,266 --> 00:11:23,633
and you’re like, "Are you on?"
I mean, what is he doing this for?

259
00:11:23,699 --> 00:11:26,000
His voice was his voice. That was him.

260
00:11:30,466 --> 00:11:32,533
I went to the Yankee game once,
World Series.

261
00:11:32,866 --> 00:11:36,733
So I’m at the game with Lorne Michaels
and with Jack Nicholson.

262
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,033
Jack Nicholson’s the coolest.

263
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:40,166
One of those guys
where his voice is his voice.

264
00:11:40,233 --> 00:11:42,633
It’s like saying,
"You’re you, he’s Jack Nicholson."

265
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:46,639
So we order a hot dog
and beer, and I get Cracker Jacks.

266
00:11:46,733 --> 00:11:49,400
I’m eating Cracker Jacks,
and he looks at me,

267
00:11:49,442 --> 00:11:50,843
he’s got sunglasses, and he goes,

268
00:11:51,644 --> 00:11:53,779
[imitating Nicholson]
"Did you get the prize yet?"

269
00:11:53,933 --> 00:11:58,233
And I go-- I swear to God...
I get it out, I open up the prize.

270
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,133
It’s a sticker, a picture of a snake.

271
00:12:01,199 --> 00:12:03,100
He goes, "You know, when I was a kid,

272
00:12:03,166 --> 00:12:07,466
we used to get metal things,
like tin whistles, stuff like that."

273
00:12:07,533 --> 00:12:08,766
Then without even looking at me,

274
00:12:08,833 --> 00:12:10,500
he’s looking out at the game,
he goes,

275
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:12,898
"Now you get a picture of
a [bleeps] snake."

276
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:17,100
Dude, it was like someone wrote it
in the scripts.

277
00:12:17,166 --> 00:12:19,333
"Now you get a picture of
a [bleeps] snake."

278
00:12:19,766 --> 00:12:22,900
The funniest part is that
he asked you about the prize,

279
00:12:22,966 --> 00:12:26,966
and that he looks off.
That’s the melancholy.

280
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:28,914
-You look off into the distance.
-Looking off.

281
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:31,166
It’s all crumbling.

282
00:12:36,266 --> 00:12:38,366
-Are you finito? Or...
-Yeah, I’m done.

283
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,426
-Okay, great. Thank you so much.
-I want one more...

284
00:12:40,493 --> 00:12:43,462
-[server] Oh, my gosh.
-[Jerry and server laughing]

285
00:12:43,533 --> 00:12:46,199
-That’s it, that’s all I want. Just one--
-Is that?

286
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:49,533
Thank you, thank you. That’s it, no more.
That's fine.

287
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,033
You think I’m going to lose it, right?

288
00:12:57,099 --> 00:12:58,300
At one point, I crack.

289
00:12:58,366 --> 00:13:02,699
The talk show host's life
is a sick science experiment.

290
00:13:02,766 --> 00:13:05,300
"Let’s seal up a lovable human being,

291
00:13:05,566 --> 00:13:09,933
inside a studio and make him
make five hours of television a week.

292
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,033
And see what happens."

293
00:13:12,433 --> 00:13:15,933
"Let’s see what psychological issues,

294
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,666
personality issues, power issues--"

295
00:13:18,933 --> 00:13:20,633
It will be fun. Just for fun.

296
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:21,666
"Just for fun,

297
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:26,466
we’re going to put Jimmy Fallon
in a tube, for 30 years.

298
00:13:26,533 --> 00:13:29,766
‘Cause the human brain
has thousands of parts, like a car.

299
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:33,279
Something’s going to break.
Wonder what it will be?"

300
00:13:35,033 --> 00:13:35,966
How cruel.

301
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:40,866
Let’s get back to Sagpone. Or what is it?

302
00:13:41,466 --> 00:13:44,866
-Sagaponack. It’s Indian.
-[Jerry] Sounds like an Indian apology.

303
00:13:44,933 --> 00:13:47,000
It’s like if one Indian accidentally steps

304
00:13:47,066 --> 00:13:49,133
on another Indian’s tepee
and knocks it down,

305
00:13:49,199 --> 00:13:50,566
"Sagaponack. Oh, Sagaponack."

306
00:13:51,764 --> 00:13:55,734
If you looked it up on Wikipedia,
it means "land of the underground balls."

307
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:59,066
I think they meant potatoes.
I’m being serious.

308
00:13:59,133 --> 00:14:01,099
Oh, because there's potato farms there.

309
00:14:01,166 --> 00:14:02,233
-All potato farms.
-Yeah.

310
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:05,400
So I think that’s what they meant
by "underground balls."

311
00:14:05,466 --> 00:14:07,666
Anyways, I don’t know.
The whole thing, it is--

312
00:14:07,733 --> 00:14:09,466
Let’s hope that’s what they meant.

313
00:14:09,533 --> 00:14:10,633
Let’s hope.

314
00:14:10,699 --> 00:14:14,400
Either that or the mob got to the US
a lot earlier than we thought.

315
00:14:14,766 --> 00:14:17,199
No disrespect, Sagaponack.

316
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,199
Okay, here I go.

317
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:24,366
[woman] It’s been a pleasure.
God bless you both.

318
00:14:24,433 --> 00:14:26,233
-[Jerry] Thank you.
-[Jimmy] It was fun. Cool.

319
00:14:26,298 --> 00:14:29,301
-[woman] Keep up the good work.
-[Jimmy] Thank you. Bye, guys.

320
00:14:29,366 --> 00:14:31,066
-[brakes screech]
-[woman] He know how to drive it?

321
00:14:31,133 --> 00:14:32,599
[Jimmy] No, he’s figuring it out.

322
00:14:32,638 --> 00:14:35,708
-[woman] People usually do it for him.
-[woman 2] There’s a clutch, honey.

323
00:14:35,774 --> 00:14:40,246
-Oh, my God. It couldn’t be more perfect.
-[women shouting indistinctly]

324
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:44,250
-[Jimmy] No. He's got to jump us now.
-[Jerry] I’m on it.

325
00:14:44,433 --> 00:14:45,966
[Jimmy laughing]

326
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:48,633
Oh, my God.

327
00:14:49,033 --> 00:14:52,500
I don’t want any more.
I don’t want any more of this.

328
00:14:52,866 --> 00:14:54,699
[Jerry] I’m glad I’m with you,
you know why?

329
00:14:54,766 --> 00:14:56,500
You bring out my good side.

330
00:14:57,099 --> 00:14:59,933
I have a dark side,
but I can’t have it around you.

331
00:14:59,999 --> 00:15:03,168
Same way I had to change the impression,
I have to change my personality.

332
00:15:03,966 --> 00:15:05,099
To match yours.

333
00:15:05,337 --> 00:15:07,273
-[laughing]
-[Jimmy] Thank you.

334
00:15:09,341 --> 00:15:12,645
-[applause]
-[Jimmy cheering]

335
00:15:12,933 --> 00:15:16,833
[Jimmy] All right, that went on
for 45 seconds too long, those ladies.

336
00:15:17,016 --> 00:15:19,151
-Yep. [laughs]
-That was annoying.

337
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:21,120
Were you annoyed with those ladies?

338
00:15:21,366 --> 00:15:24,366
Uh, yeah. Completely annoyed.

339
00:15:24,733 --> 00:15:28,000
Finally, Jimmy Fallon gets annoyed.
That makes my day.

340
00:15:28,066 --> 00:15:30,433
[Jimmy] I don’t even like practical jokes.

341
00:15:30,533 --> 00:15:31,866
I don’t find them practical.

342
00:15:31,933 --> 00:15:34,433
-If someone actually did a Punk'd thing--
-Yeah.

343
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,466
Or the... I wouldn’t sign the release.
I'd go, "No."

344
00:15:37,933 --> 00:15:39,266
-Really?
-That’s how mad I am.

345
00:15:39,333 --> 00:15:42,466
So mad that you pranked me
that I’m not going to do that.

346
00:15:42,533 --> 00:15:45,800
And it’s unusable stuff.
And now the pranks on you.

347
00:15:45,866 --> 00:15:49,266
-That--
-You've wasted a whole day of pranking me.

348
00:15:54,933 --> 00:15:56,933
You know what I wanted to tell you?
I forgot.

349
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:57,833
[Jerry] What?

350
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,233
[Jimmy] I called you back.
They said, "Thanks for calling."

351
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:01,400
Or something, and I go,

352
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,461
"It’s the least I can do."

353
00:16:02,828 --> 00:16:05,230
And you go, "What is that?
'The least I can do'?

354
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:07,666
Why would you say, 'It’s the least--'
Like, thanks a lot."

355
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:08,566
Right.

356
00:16:08,633 --> 00:16:11,966
[Jimmy] I texted you dates I could do it
and maybe some suggestions

357
00:16:12,033 --> 00:16:13,733
of different cars you might want to do.

358
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:14,633
[Jerry] Yeah, yeah.

359
00:16:14,699 --> 00:16:16,433
And you didn’t text or call me back.

360
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:18,666
No, that’s the least I could do.

361
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,900
-You actually did the least you could do.
-Yes.

362
00:16:23,966 --> 00:16:24,900
-Yes.
-Oh, my God.

363
00:16:24,966 --> 00:16:26,633
-It’s to show you.
-I didn’t do the...

364
00:16:26,699 --> 00:16:27,566
-No.
-No.

365
00:16:27,633 --> 00:16:29,933
I called you and said,
"This is the least I can do."

366
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,533
I thought it was the least I could do,
to call you back.

367
00:16:32,599 --> 00:16:33,500
Yeah, no.

368
00:16:33,566 --> 00:16:35,333
I wanted to show you
that’s not the least.

369
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:39,300
The least he can do is exactly, you know.

370
00:16:39,366 --> 00:16:40,733
[Jerry] Yeah. "I’ll show this guy."

371
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:43,533
[Jimmy] Show me what’s what.

372
00:16:51,366 --> 00:16:54,833
[Jimmy] You know, I snuck on to the set
of your last episode.

373
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,199
-[Jerry] Oh, you did?
-Yeah.

374
00:16:56,266 --> 00:17:00,833
No one checked us for tickets. And we
just walked in. And we sat in the crowd.

375
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:03,633
I have a photograph of me
and Dom Irrera in your kitchen.

376
00:17:04,033 --> 00:17:06,866
And so, I took a toothbrush
out of your bathroom.

377
00:17:07,826 --> 00:17:09,595
The blue toothbrush with white bristles.

378
00:17:09,666 --> 00:17:12,000
-Do you still have it?
-I have it in a safe place,

379
00:17:12,066 --> 00:17:13,500
-in a box somewhere.
-That’s so fun.

380
00:17:13,566 --> 00:17:15,733
And I owe it to you,
you’ll get it before--

381
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:16,633
I don’t want it.

382
00:17:16,668 --> 00:17:19,805
-What do you mean, you have to have it.
-No, it’s yours. You stole it.

383
00:17:21,507 --> 00:17:24,777
It’s like the Born to Run thing.
[imitating Jerry] He doesn’t want it.

384
00:17:24,943 --> 00:17:26,912
[Jimmy] "What am I going to do
with it? I’m stuck with it.

385
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,600
It’s not who wants it,
it’s who gets stuck with it."

